From 3302b2c0243b58cd5ece88a5177a34f019e1bb8c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: aliosa27 <aliosa27@aliosa27.me>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 12:43:27 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 28/28] Station side: DHCP server on the fallback address while
 there is no WiFi link

After 60 s without a lease the device already falls back to 192.168.123.1.
A station with no link now also serves DHCP there (192.168.123.100-200,
router/DNS 192.168.123.1, 2-minute leases), so a PC cabled straight to it
gets an address. Stopped when the link comes up (events.c) or a lease
arrives, so it never competes with a real server across the bridge.
---
 NOTES.md         |  2 +-
 project/events.c |  1 +
 project/main.c   | 43 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 project/syscfg.h |  1 +
 4 files changed, 45 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

