@@ -21,7 +21,7 @@ Taixin TXW8301 (TXW4002A, C-SKY CK803) HaLow wireless-bridge (WNB) firmware SDK
 
 ## Code map
 
-- `main.c`: init order (`sys_cfg_load` → role key → WiFi → network → `sys_app_init`), DHCP server start, 1 s main loop. It `#include`s `atcmd.c`. `sys_dhcpc_check()` (main loop) also does the DHCP fallback: with the DHCP client on and no lease (`dhcp_supplied_address`) for 60 s, `w0` gets 192.168.123.1/24 (fixed, not `sys_cfgs.ipaddr`) and DHCP is restarted; a later lease replaces it. Note `events.c` still copies each lease into `sys_cfgs.ipaddr`, which is the boot address until the fallback kicks in.
+- `main.c`: init order (`sys_cfg_load` → role key → WiFi → network → `sys_app_init`), DHCP server start, 1 s main loop. It `#include`s `atcmd.c`. `sys_dhcpc_check()` (main loop) also does the DHCP fallback: with the DHCP client on and no lease (`dhcp_supplied_address`) for 60 s, `w0` gets 192.168.123.1/24 (fixed, not `sys_cfgs.ipaddr`) and DHCP is restarted; a later lease replaces it. Note `events.c` still copies each lease into `sys_cfgs.ipaddr`, which is the boot address until the fallback kicks in. On the station side, while `w0` is on the fallback address and there is no WiFi link, `sys_fallback_dhcpd()` also runs the DHCP server (192.168.123.100–200, router and DNS 192.168.123.1, 2-minute leases), so a PC cabled straight to the device gets an address. It stops when a lease arrives, and on `SYSEVT_WIFI_CONNECTTED` (`events.c`) so it never serves DHCP across the bridge. Verified on hardware (2026-11-22).
 - `syscfg.c`/`syscfg.h`: `sys_cfgs` defaults, `wificfg_flush()` (pushes config to an interface), `syscfg_flush()` (restart WiFi with current config), mode enum (`STA=1`, `WNBSTA=2`, `AP=3`, `WNBAP=4`, repeater modes from `AP_STA=5`). The mode number is also the interface index (`wificfg_get_ifidx`).
 - `sdk/lib/common/atcmd.c`: source for the `sys_wifi_atcmd_*` handlers, the reference for how to change settings correctly (channel = 1-based index into `chan_list`, bandwidth ∈ {1,2,4,8} MHz, `chan_list` in 100 kHz units, PSK via `wpa_passphrase`).
 - `project_config.h` overrides the defaults in `sys_config.h` (`#ifndef` pattern). With `ROLE_KEY_EN`, GPIO `PA_8` picks the AP or STA side at boot (high = AP) and overrides the saved side. It keeps the saved type: `ap` and `sta` stay standard, `wnbap` and `wnbsta` stay WNB (`sys_role_key_init` in `main.c`). Repeater modes ignore the pin.
diff --git a/project/events.c b/project/events.c
index 0400e62..7c18bb7 100644
--- a/project/events.c
+++ b/project/events.c
@@ -57,6 +57,7 @@ sysevt_hdl_res sys_event_hdl(uint32 event_id, uint32 data, uint32 priv)
         case SYS_EVENT(SYS_EVENT_WIFI, SYSEVT_WIFI_CONNECTTED):
             sys_status.wifi_connected = 1;
 #if SYS_NETWORK_SUPPORT
